.TH INPUT.H 3v32 "October 11, 2026" "Vircon32 DevTools 26.04.24" "Vircon32 C Library"
.SH NAME
input.h \- Vircon32 gamepads: directions and buttons
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqinput.h\(dq
.PP
.BI "void select_gamepad( int " gamepad_id " );"
.B  "int  get_selected_gamepad();"
.B  "bool gamepad_is_connected();"
.PP
.B  "int  gamepad_left();"
.B  "int  gamepad_right();"
.B  "int  gamepad_up();"
.B  "int  gamepad_down();"
.BI "void gamepad_direction( int* " delta_x ", int* " delta_y " );"
.BI "void gamepad_direction_normalized( float* " delta_x ", float* " delta_y " );"
.PP
.B  "int  gamepad_button_a();"
.B  "int  gamepad_button_b();"
.B  "int  gamepad_button_x();"
.B  "int  gamepad_button_y();"
.B  "int  gamepad_button_l();"
.B  "int  gamepad_button_r();"
.B  "int  gamepad_button_start();"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The console has 4 gamepad ports, ids 0 to 3 (the emulator's menus
call them gamepads 1 to 4). Each gamepad has a D-pad, buttons A, B, X,
Y, L and R, and Start. All the reading functions apply to the selected
gamepad.
.PP
The state of the gamepads changes only between frames, so reading the
same control twice within a frame gives the same answer.
.TP
.BR select_gamepad ", " get_selected_gamepad
Select the gamepad to read. Gamepad 0 is selected at power-on. An id
outside 0 to 3 is ignored.
.TP
.B gamepad_is_connected
Whether a controller is connected to the selected port.
.SS Reading a control
Each direction and button function returns a count of frames:
.TP
.RI "a positive " n
the control is pressed, and has been for
.I n
frames (1 on the first frame it is pressed);
.TP
.RI "a negative " n
the control is released, and has been for
.RI \- n
frames (\-1 on the first frame after it was released).
.PP
So
.B "> 0"
means \(lqheld\(rq,
.B "== 1"
means \(lqjust pressed\(rq and
.B "== \-1"
means \(lqjust released\(rq. The counts stop at 3600 and \-3600 (one
minute). A gamepad that is not connected reports every control as
released for \-3600 frames. Opposite directions are never both
pressed: pressing one releases the other.
.TP
.B gamepad_direction
Store \-1, 0 or 1 in each of
.I *delta_x
and
.I *delta_y
from the D-pad (left and up are \-1).
.TP
.B gamepad_direction_normalized
The same as floats, scaled to length 1 on diagonals (each component
becomes \(+-0.7071).
.SH EXAMPLES
Jump only when A is first pressed, not while it is held:
.PP
.RS
.nf
#include "input.h"

bool jump_requested()
{
    select_gamepad( 0 );
    return gamepad_button_a() == 1;
}
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vircon32 (3v32),
.BR time.h (3v32),
.BR Vircon32 (1),
.BR input.hpp (3v32)
.SH AUTHOR
The Vircon32 standard library was written by Javier Carracedo
.RI ( Carra ).
